CORE
reset6.sv
--module top --bound 5 --reset top.counter
^the reset condition reads no input, and is hence imposed on the initial state only$
^\[top\.assert\.1\] top\.counter != 0: PROVED up to bound 5$
^\[top\.assert\.2\] always top\.counter != 3: REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The reset condition reads no input. It is imposed on the initial state;
its negation was required in every later state as well, which no path
with more than two states satisfies, as counter is incremented, and every
property was hence proved vacuously.
